00:27:32.651 --> 00:27:33.652
What's the source?

00:27:34.528 --> 00:27:35.529
Cambodia.

00:27:36.196 --> 00:27:38.699
Hold up. Is this about the recent leak?

00:27:40.492 --> 00:27:41.493
Yeah.

00:27:43.620 --> 00:27:47.708
So, it is stolen goods. That's bold.

00:27:48.333 --> 00:27:52.003
Well, Interpol's lost the trace.

00:27:52.004 --> 00:27:55.299
No records left in any account. It's clean.

00:27:55.841 --> 00:28:01.346
At the price from two years ago, I'd say it's a win-win for both sides.

00:28:02.264 --> 00:28:04.224
I would like to see the real thing first.

00:28:05.851 --> 00:28:07.102
When are you coming over?

00:28:08.562 --> 00:28:09.897
I will let you know.

00:28:11.189 --> 00:28:12.190
Okay.

00:28:24.578 --> 00:28:29.707
WHERE ARE YOU? ABOUT CAMBODIA...

00:28:29.708 --> 00:28:31.084
INCOMING VOICE CALL

00:28:31.919 --> 00:28:33.462
Heeju, where are you?

00:28:34.171 --> 00:28:36.381
I just talked to the people who are gonna buy our gold.

00:28:37.174 --> 00:28:39.343
We should be able to get a good price for all the bars.

00:28:41.595 --> 00:28:43.429
Good job, Heeju.

00:28:43.430 --> 00:28:44.514
It's over.

00:28:45.265 --> 00:28:47.683
We can just start our new lives together.

00:28:51.229 --> 00:28:52.813
You still there?

00:28:52.814 --> 00:28:54.274
Heeju, did you hear me?

00:28:55.817 --> 00:28:57.861
- I'm here. -  Okay.

00:28:58.612 --> 00:28:59.863
You heard what I said, right?

00:29:03.617 --> 00:29:05.535
They murdered Cha Yujin.

00:29:06.870 --> 00:29:08.663
Yeah, I know.

00:29:08.664 --> 00:29:10.999
That asshole Park called and tried to blackmail me.

00:29:16.129 --> 00:29:17.172
But it's okay.

00:29:17.965 --> 00:29:19.466
We've got nothing to worry about.

00:29:20.258 --> 00:29:24.345
I have other contacts at airport security so moving the gold shouldn't be a problem.

00:29:24.346 --> 00:29:26.431
Our Cambodian buyers said they'd help, too.

00:29:27.683 --> 00:29:29.684
Cha Yujin told me everything.

00:29:29.685 --> 00:29:31.936
About how you two used to be together.

00:29:31.937 --> 00:29:33.729
It didn't mean anything, Heeju.

00:29:33.730 --> 00:29:36.023
I don't know what she told you, but you're different.

00:29:36.024 --> 00:29:37.358
It's different with us.

00:29:37.359 --> 00:29:39.735
Sh-she's just-she's nothing to me.

00:29:39.736 --> 00:29:41.530
Someone close to you just died.

00:29:42.614 --> 00:29:45.325
And it's okay because someone else can help with shipping?

00:29:50.330 --> 00:29:51.623
I guess you were right.

00:29:53.208 --> 00:29:55.918
Cha Yujin really meant nothing to you at all.

00:29:55.919 --> 00:29:57.753
That's what I was trying to tell you.

00:29:57.754 --> 00:29:59.296
No one else matters.

00:29:59.297 --> 00:30:00.424
:cue

00:30:01.299 --> 00:30:02.843
You're different from all of them.

00:30:12.769 --> 00:30:14.521
I think I've gone too far.

00:30:15.981 --> 00:30:18.400
Where are you now? I can come find you.

00:30:19.443 --> 00:30:21.194
I don't think I can see you today.

00:30:21.987 --> 00:30:24.364
I'm sorry. I'll call you later.

00:30:28.285 --> 00:30:29.286
Wait.

00:31:01.359 --> 00:31:04.738
GANGWON SAEBAEK HOSPITAL

00:31:50.909 --> 00:31:52.410
What have you been doing?

00:31:55.622 --> 00:31:56.748
Auntie.

00:31:59.417 --> 00:32:01.920
Let me sleep here just tonight.

00:32:06.925 --> 00:32:08.468
I'm so tired.

00:32:15.517 --> 00:32:16.810
That's what it is.

00:32:18.395 --> 00:32:20.230
You smell like a coal mine.

00:32:25.068 --> 00:32:27.195
That damp coal smell.

00:32:29.156 --> 00:32:31.533
The one that miners have on their clothes.

00:32:45.172 --> 00:32:48.257
JEIL WORKSHOP

00:33:24.628 --> 00:33:25.629
Hoonseok?

00:33:29.174 --> 00:33:30.175
You brought it.

00:33:33.094 --> 00:33:34.095
Yeah.

00:33:35.138 --> 00:33:37.432
And the rest of the gold bars.

00:33:39.392 --> 00:33:40.810
Where are they?

00:33:49.945 --> 00:33:51.071
Tell me.

00:33:51.947 --> 00:33:53.531
Where did you hide the gold bars? :cue

00:33:55.325 --> 00:33:56.576
I'm gonna shoot.

00:33:58.328 --> 00:33:59.871
Three.

00:34:04.626 --> 00:34:05.919
Two.

00:34:06.795 --> 00:34:08.129
One.

00:34:16.972 --> 00:34:18.222
Good.

00:34:18.223 --> 00:34:20.182
Good, you got it now. No matter what happens,

00:34:20.183 --> 00:34:22.560
you never tell anybody where the bars are.

00:34:23.520 --> 00:34:25.939
Seriously, Heeju, if I wanted to I could've just...

00:34:26.773 --> 00:34:29.067
...I mean, how the hell could you even think of betraying me like that?

00:34:40.745 --> 00:34:41.871
Look.

00:34:42.622 --> 00:34:44.165
This potato's what saved your life.

00:34:46.876 --> 00:34:48.878
So did you meet up with Lee Dokyung?

00:34:50.213 --> 00:34:51.298
I didn't.

00:34:53.049 --> 00:34:54.050
Why not?

00:34:55.468 --> 00:34:57.304
Because I can't trust anyone.

00:34:57.804 --> 00:34:59.306
Not anymore.

00:35:00.223 --> 00:35:01.349
Wait a sec.

00:35:02.892 --> 00:35:05.770
So you're not going with Lee Dokyung? Did you end things?

00:35:07.689 --> 00:35:11.484
Yes! Good job, Heeju! You finally got it!

00:35:12.193 --> 00:35:14.403
Hell, you can't trust a guy like him!

00:35:14.404 --> 00:35:17.281
Heh, I was trying to tell you that this whole time, and I-

00:35:17.282 --> 00:35:18.283
wait a minute.

00:35:19.409 --> 00:35:21.995
The thing is, you still have all the gold bars.

00:35:22.621 --> 00:35:24.331
Is Dokyung really just gonna walk away?

00:35:24.956 --> 00:35:27.125
Ah, shit. Do I need to kill him?

00:35:27.709 --> 00:35:29.836
Don't think that I trust you, either.

00:35:31.630 --> 00:35:32.631
Okay.

00:35:33.923 --> 00:35:34.924
Be that way.

00:35:35.425 --> 00:35:36.426
You just use me.

00:35:37.093 --> 00:35:38.345
Keep on using me.

00:35:39.346 --> 00:35:40.764
As much as you want.

00:35:41.348 --> 00:35:42.807
Happy to be of service.

00:35:43.475 --> 00:35:47.186
For every two ten-kilo bars, I get one one-kilo bar.

00:35:47.187 --> 00:35:48.188
Just one.

00:35:48.772 --> 00:35:50.273
Not too much, right?

00:35:50.940 --> 00:35:52.817
Oh, yeah. That reminds me.

00:35:53.193 --> 00:35:56.071
I did the math and it should take us about six months to sell them all.

00:35:56.571 --> 00:35:57.572
Six.

00:36:00.784 --> 00:36:02.326
Park knows about me now.

00:36:02.327 --> 00:36:04.828
That means soon your whole company will, too.

00:36:04.829 --> 00:36:07.165
Not to mention the police on top of that.

00:36:08.708 --> 00:36:10.751
And you're telling me we have to last six more months?

00:36:10.752 --> 00:36:12.879
No. They don't know.

00:36:13.296 --> 00:36:15.048
Park? He doesn't know.

00:36:17.008 --> 00:36:19.177
Cha Yujin must have told Park about me.

00:36:19.719 --> 00:36:22.138
The gold bars, everything. He must know.

00:36:24.933 --> 00:36:26.642
If Park had known it was you,

00:36:26.643 --> 00:36:28.478
he wouldn't have gone to the mine.

00:36:28.853 --> 00:36:30.563
He would have gone to the pawnshop.

00:36:32.565 --> 00:36:35.067
So now here's the real question.

00:36:37.362 --> 00:36:40.240
Park was alone. Why?

00:36:40.740 --> 00:36:42.533
After he killed Cha Yujin,

00:36:42.534 --> 00:36:44.993
he went to the mine alone without telling anyone.

00:36:44.994 --> 00:36:45.995
Why did he do that?

00:36:48.915 --> 00:36:50.083
Because that way...

00:36:51.835 --> 00:36:54.838
- ...he could keep all the gold. - Bingo.

00:36:55.463 --> 00:36:57.256
And he didn't want Chairman Ahn to find out.

00:36:57.257 --> 00:36:58.299
Chairman Ahn?

00:36:59.843 --> 00:37:00.844
The real owner of the gold.

00:37:03.638 --> 00:37:06.057
Geumseong's chair, Ahn Gyuseok.

00:37:07.142 --> 00:37:09.519
Chairman Ahn gets back to Korea today.

00:37:11.229 --> 00:37:12.939
And that means Park is fucked.

00:37:14.107 --> 00:37:15.190
Welcome back, Chairman.

00:37:15.191 --> 00:37:16.526
Welcome back, sir!

00:37:17.277 --> 00:37:20.571
These are our partners from Cambodia. Our executives.

00:37:20.572 --> 00:37:22.114
- Introduce yourselves. - Yes, sir.

00:37:22.115 --> 00:37:24.408
- Director Jo. - Thank you for coming all this way.

00:37:24.409 --> 00:37:26.201
These guys here, take care of 'em.

00:37:26.202 --> 00:37:27.745
- Nice to meet you. - Give them anything they want.

00:37:27.746 --> 00:37:29.663
- You understand? Only the best. - Of course, sir.

00:37:29.664 --> 00:37:30.915
This way, please.

00:37:33.626 --> 00:37:34.918
- Come here. - Sir.

00:37:34.919 --> 00:37:35.962
What is this?

00:37:36.921 --> 00:37:38.006
Be more subtle.

00:37:39.132 --> 00:37:40.759
Apologies. :cue

00:37:52.812 --> 00:37:54.022
Hey, step on it.

00:37:54.522 --> 00:37:58.026
My stomach is starting to hurt from all that greasy food I had to eat.

00:38:04.324 --> 00:38:06.493
Do I really have to ask about it?

00:38:07.368 --> 00:38:08.661
Right, yes.

00:38:10.830 --> 00:38:13.583
- So, Lee Dokyung, he- - Managed to escape from the hospital.

00:38:16.544 --> 00:38:18.086
You're kidding, right?

00:38:18.087 --> 00:38:20.214
Why did I have to hear that from someone else?

00:38:20.215 --> 00:38:21.882
It seemed like you had a busy schedule,

00:38:21.883 --> 00:38:24.718
so I was planning to report it to you when you got back.

00:38:24.719 --> 00:38:27.054
You do not make decisions for me.

00:38:27.055 --> 00:38:28.431
Yes, sir.

00:38:30.391 --> 00:38:31.476
So the casket.

00:38:32.018 --> 00:38:34.395
Is it waiting for us at the hotel?

00:38:35.688 --> 00:38:37.232
I'm sorry, sir.

00:38:38.441 --> 00:38:40.777
Enough with the apologizing "I'm sorry" shit.

00:38:42.904 --> 00:38:45.031
You should know me better than anyone else by now.

00:38:46.157 --> 00:38:48.742
Have I ever said anything about all the bullshit,

00:38:48.743 --> 00:38:51.204
or the way you all stab each other in the back?

00:38:51.746 --> 00:38:54.206
There's only one thing I can't forgive.

00:38:54.207 --> 00:38:57.293
And that's any damage to the company. I will not let that happen.

00:38:59.295 --> 00:39:00.547
I take responsibility.

00:39:02.090 --> 00:39:03.424
I'll find the casket, sir.

00:39:06.052 --> 00:39:07.303
It's too late now.

00:39:20.900 --> 00:39:24.444
H.S HOTEL & RESORT CONSTRUCTION

00:39:42.422 --> 00:39:45.716
Huh, you know, maybe we dug a little too deep.

00:39:46.926 --> 00:39:48.094
Hey, Park Hocheol.

00:39:50.263 --> 00:39:53.056
Look where you are. Shit.

00:39:53.057 --> 00:39:54.434
Think carefully, now.

00:39:56.394 --> 00:39:58.730
How did you know what was in the casket?

00:39:59.272 --> 00:40:00.857
Kim Jinman, he...

00:40:01.816 --> 00:40:03.067
...he told me.

00:40:03.776 --> 00:40:05.110
Ah.

00:40:05.111 --> 00:40:07.655
So the police already found out about it.

00:40:08.823 --> 00:40:10.867
And you decided not to tell me.

00:40:11.451 --> 00:40:12.911
You didn't bring it up.

00:40:13.328 --> 00:40:14.411
So that meant-

00:40:18.625 --> 00:40:20.834
So that meant I couldn't-

00:40:20.835 --> 00:40:22.085
I couldn't tell you.

00:40:24.047 --> 00:40:26.256
That's not the reason.

00:40:26.257 --> 00:40:29.427
Otherwise, you would have just asked me about it.

00:40:31.262 --> 00:40:33.764
Were you planning to find it and take it for yourself?

00:40:35.308 --> 00:40:37.810
Or did you already do it, and now you're lying?

00:40:38.144 --> 00:40:39.979
Did you plan this with Lee Dokyung?

00:40:41.147 --> 00:40:43.106
No. No, sir.

00:40:43.107 --> 00:40:44.399
Right.

00:40:44.400 --> 00:40:46.736
Because if you had, you wouldn't still be in Geumseong.

00:40:51.699 --> 00:40:53.826
You probably would have fled already.

00:40:55.495 --> 00:40:57.413
Stay out of the business with the casket.

00:40:58.623 --> 00:41:01.626
Go back to Yes Money and keep doing what you used to do. :cue

00:41:03.169 --> 00:41:05.671
Say hi to the shareholders at Gold Land.

00:41:05.672 --> 00:41:07.382
Get 'em to sign that contract.

00:41:08.883 --> 00:41:12.803
Yeah, the more I think about it, it's all you're really cut out for.

00:41:14.973 --> 00:41:16.182
Get him out.

00:41:18.059 --> 00:41:21.562
Fuck, I must be getting old now. I'm getting a bit soft, huh?

00:41:24.774 --> 00:41:26.484
You know what?

00:41:27.402 --> 00:41:29.695
You should have reported this whole thing right away.

00:41:29.696 --> 00:41:32.156
Coulda avoided the Chairman's wrath.

00:41:35.910 --> 00:41:37.912
You got pretty lucky in the end, though.

00:41:38.329 --> 00:41:40.288
I mean, he wanted to cut your ear off.

00:41:40.289 --> 00:41:41.708
I barely talked him out of it.

00:41:42.750 --> 00:41:44.876
Mm, from now on,

00:41:44.877 --> 00:41:47.296
you should keep your head down at Yes Money. Gimmie that.

00:41:48.006 --> 00:41:50.633
I'll take care of the gold bars, okay? Here.

00:41:51.134 --> 00:41:52.301
Come on, Park.

00:41:53.344 --> 00:41:55.513
How did you know about the gold bars?

00:41:56.514 --> 00:41:58.640
I was in Yangpo then, wasn't I?

00:42:00.268 --> 00:42:02.520
I sent the casket. I've always known.

00:42:03.187 --> 00:42:06.773
You've lost your fucking touch, you know know that?

00:42:08.943 --> 00:42:10.570
You don't know your place.

00:42:11.529 --> 00:42:13.113
Hey, here you go.

00:42:14.449 --> 00:42:15.742
Good luck getting out of there!

00:43:09.378 --> 00:43:11.130
Park isn't the only one.

00:43:11.631 --> 00:43:13.590
I think someone else saw me, too.

00:43:13.591 --> 00:43:15.134
What do you mean? Who saw you?

00:43:16.427 --> 00:43:17.428
Kim Jinman.

00:43:19.055 --> 00:43:21.599
I think he saw me getting into my car that night.

00:43:22.850 --> 00:43:26.144
When I was running away from the Jeongsan nightclub with Cha Yujin.

00:43:26.145 --> 00:43:27.896
Listen to me! Open the door!

00:43:27.897 --> 00:43:30.107
Look, look, look! Roll, roll, roll down your window!

00:43:30.108 --> 00:43:32.526
He must not have seen you 'cause he would have reported you

00:43:32.527 --> 00:43:33.945
to my company right away.

00:43:34.987 --> 00:43:36.280
Yeah, but you know...

00:43:37.156 --> 00:43:40.283
...what if he's not saying anything because he wants the gold for himself?

00:43:40.284 --> 00:43:42.285
Park never said anything, either.

00:43:42.286 --> 00:43:43.913
Ah, shit.

00:43:46.749 --> 00:43:47.750
Heeju.

00:43:48.417 --> 00:43:51.295
Your old phone and credit card. You threw those away, right?

00:43:53.881 --> 00:43:55.508
Then you got no choice.

00:43:57.510 --> 00:43:59.637
You have to be Ju Haran for the rest of your life.

00:44:02.431 --> 00:44:04.225
Don't worry about it.

00:44:05.268 --> 00:44:06.727
If Detective Kim finds out...

00:44:07.478 --> 00:44:09.188
...then I'll simply go and kill him for you.

00:44:10.690 --> 00:44:12.358
Then you can give me an extra potato.

00:44:14.402 --> 00:44:15.403
Deal? :cue

00:44:19.365 --> 00:44:20.448
Hello.

00:44:28.875 --> 00:44:30.585
Hi, there. Hey.

00:44:31.252 --> 00:44:33.128
Uh, room five.

00:44:33.129 --> 00:44:35.172
Was Yeo Sunok discharged already?

00:44:35.173 --> 00:44:37.800
Uh, no. She was moved to a private room.

00:44:38.426 --> 00:44:39.594
- She was? -  Yes.

00:44:41.846 --> 00:44:43.306
Wow, so pretty!

00:44:45.641 --> 00:44:47.309
Now, here.

00:44:47.310 --> 00:44:48.560
Ah!

00:44:48.561 --> 00:44:51.438
Oh, wow. What a nice room you got here.

00:44:51.439 --> 00:44:52.564
- Huh? -  Sorry, who-

00:44:52.565 --> 00:44:54.734
-  Must be pretty expensive. -  Who are you?

00:44:55.067 --> 00:44:56.151
Oh.

00:44:56.152 --> 00:44:57.278
Is he from the ER?

00:44:57.778 --> 00:45:00.281
- Could you just give us a second? -  Hmm?

00:45:01.991 --> 00:45:02.992
Oh.

00:45:06.120 --> 00:45:09.706
This really is a nice room. Wow.

00:45:10.958 --> 00:45:13.544
When were you put in here? Damn, look at this view.

00:45:14.253 --> 00:45:15.838
Isn't it too expensive, though?

00:45:16.339 --> 00:45:17.505
Why are you here?

00:45:17.506 --> 00:45:19.507
Just wanted to say hi to an old friend.

00:45:19.508 --> 00:45:20.717
Can't a guy do that?

00:45:20.718 --> 00:45:23.638
Who knows? We might not have much time left.

00:45:24.472 --> 00:45:26.640
I'm not just talkin' about you.

00:45:26.641 --> 00:45:30.310
I mean, at our age, who doesn't have some kind of illness or some other kinda shit?

00:45:30.311 --> 00:45:32.103
I got diabetes.

00:45:32.104 --> 00:45:33.772
And my liver's not great, either.

00:45:33.773 --> 00:45:36.191
I could go any day now, you know?

00:45:39.487 --> 00:45:40.779
Hey.

00:45:40.780 --> 00:45:42.572
Isn't it weird we both live in Jeongsan

00:45:42.573 --> 00:45:44.741
but we've never run into each other before now?

00:45:44.742 --> 00:45:46.786
More like we pretended not to.

00:45:47.536 --> 00:45:49.663
I saw you a couple times.

00:45:49.664 --> 00:45:50.831
Why didn't you say anything?

00:45:52.917 --> 00:45:54.377
What's the point in that?

00:45:55.294 --> 00:45:57.212
There's nothing left between us.

00:46:00.341 --> 00:46:01.342
And your husband?

00:46:02.134 --> 00:46:03.261
Has he come to see you?

00:46:04.387 --> 00:46:05.930
No, he hasn't.

00:46:06.889 --> 00:46:09.057
Well, still, doesn't seem like he's that bad of a guy.

00:46:09.058 --> 00:46:10.393
I mean, he even dropped the charges...

00:46:13.187 --> 00:46:15.564
If you're done saying hi, you should just go.

00:46:16.274 --> 00:46:19.359
Instead of hanging around here, dredging up old memories.

00:46:19.360 --> 00:46:21.445
Ah, come on, now. Don't be like that.

00:46:23.447 --> 00:46:25.032
Oh, by the way. Who is Ju Haran?

00:46:25.825 --> 00:46:28.618
I asked at the front desk and the receptionist said Ju Haran

00:46:28.619 --> 00:46:30.705
is your guardian, but I thought it'd be Han Cheoljung.

00:46:31.622 --> 00:46:32.706
I don't know.

00:46:32.707 --> 00:46:34.249
What do you mean? It's your guardian.

00:46:34.250 --> 00:46:35.626
Don't tell me you don't know.

00:46:37.878 --> 00:46:39.088
Here, wait.

00:46:40.381 --> 00:46:41.382
Look at this.

00:46:42.258 --> 00:46:43.259
It's her.

00:46:43.926 --> 00:46:45.011
Yeah.

00:46:45.720 --> 00:46:46.721
Right?

00:46:47.763 --> 00:46:49.806
Must be. Yeah.

00:46:49.807 --> 00:46:52.601
I remember seeing her here the other day when I came to visit you.

00:46:53.561 --> 00:46:54.936
It is her, right?

00:46:56.355 --> 00:46:57.731
But then I thought,

00:46:57.732 --> 00:47:00.901
"This woman's name is Kim Heeju, right?"

00:47:01.527 --> 00:47:02.652
Who is she?

00:47:02.653 --> 00:47:03.696
Your daughter?

00:47:04.780 --> 00:47:05.781
No.

00:47:06.240 --> 00:47:07.574
My niece.

00:47:07.575 --> 00:47:08.617
Your niece?

00:47:09.368 --> 00:47:11.203
I didn't know that you had a niece.

00:47:11.746 --> 00:47:13.956
- I do. -  I see.

00:47:14.540 --> 00:47:18.002
Oh, so then your niece, she must be pretty well-off, right?

00:47:18.961 --> 00:47:20.378
She got you into this fancy room

00:47:20.379 --> 00:47:21.672
and already took care of your hospital bills.

00:47:23.132 --> 00:47:24.507
Where does she live?

00:47:24.508 --> 00:47:25.884
Jeongsan?

00:47:25.885 --> 00:47:27.303
When is she back?

00:47:28.262 --> 00:47:29.263
I don't know.

00:47:30.556 --> 00:47:32.975
She stopped by when she heard I was sick.

00:47:33.684 --> 00:47:34.769
Why do you ask?

00:47:35.811 --> 00:47:38.646
Why do you wanna know when she'll be here?

00:47:38.647 --> 00:47:41.108
Well, you told me she's your niece, so I'd like to meet her.

00:47:41.942 --> 00:47:43.235
What? Why?

00:47:43.819 --> 00:47:45.488
Has she been gambling or something?

00:47:45.988 --> 00:47:47.280
Is she in trouble?

00:47:47.281 --> 00:47:48.282
No.

00:47:49.075 --> 00:47:50.284
Then...

00:47:50.951 --> 00:47:53.204
...did she murder someone or anything like that?

00:47:53.621 --> 00:47:56.289
Come on. What an awful thing to say.

00:47:56.290 --> 00:47:57.749
Nothing like that.

00:47:57.750 --> 00:47:59.627
No, she just borrowed some money.

00:48:00.628 --> 00:48:02.295
- How much was it? -  A lot.

00:48:02.296 --> 00:48:03.798
Actually...

00:48:04.590 --> 00:48:06.175
...it's not just about the money.

00:48:06.967 --> 00:48:09.637
Though I'd hate for someone her age to end up with a criminal record.

00:48:10.096 --> 00:48:11.971
It's not too late for her to pay it back.

00:48:11.972 --> 00:48:13.973
Or if that's not possible,

00:48:13.974 --> 00:48:16.309
then she could try and reach some kind of settlement at least.

00:48:16.310 --> 00:48:19.271
Looks like she turned off her phone, and disappeared instead.

00:48:20.398 --> 00:48:21.565
That's why I brought her up.

00:48:22.066 --> 00:48:24.401
So if she calls you or comes to visit,

00:48:24.402 --> 00:48:25.903
please be sure to let me know.

00:48:26.529 --> 00:48:28.613
I'll be more than happy to help her settle the matter.

00:48:28.614 --> 00:48:29.740
All right?

00:48:30.282 --> 00:48:31.699
Don't tell her I was here, though.

00:48:31.700 --> 00:48:34.120
If she knows the police are involved, she won't show up.

00:48:37.540 --> 00:48:41.168
There's nothing to worry about, hmm? I won't do anything to your niece.

00:48:41.627 --> 00:48:44.421
-  Call me, okay? -  Ms. Yeo Sunok?

00:48:44.422 --> 00:48:45.923
I need to check your temperature.

00:48:46.882 --> 00:48:47.883
:cue

00:48:49.093 --> 00:48:50.094
Huh?

00:48:54.390 --> 00:48:57.183
All right. I'll head out now.

00:48:57.184 --> 00:48:58.978
You'll give me a call, right?

00:48:59.937 --> 00:49:00.938
Yeah.

00:49:02.731 --> 00:49:04.692
Take care of yourself. Get some rest.

00:50:01.499 --> 00:50:03.125
Hey, Heeju. Where are you?

00:50:06.212 --> 00:50:07.837
- Uh, Dokyung- -  Tell me where you are

00:50:07.838 --> 00:50:09.340
and I'll come find you so we can talk.

00:50:17.473 --> 00:50:19.390
I'm not really sure that's a good idea.

00:50:21.894 --> 00:50:24.480
Do you think we can go back to how things used to be?

00:50:25.481 --> 00:50:26.607
What do you mean?

00:50:27.858 --> 00:50:30.109
Is it-is this because of the whole Cha Yujin thing

00:50:30.110 --> 00:50:31.570
because I never told you about her?

00:50:36.158 --> 00:50:37.867
You're right.

00:50:37.868 --> 00:50:40.246
I took advantage of a woman I was dating, but Heeju...

00:50:41.121 --> 00:50:42.498
...it's different with us.

00:50:44.083 --> 00:50:45.251
I think that...

00:50:46.252 --> 00:50:49.004
...I was actually the one taking advantage of you.

00:50:49.797 --> 00:50:50.798
When we first met...

00:50:51.757 --> 00:50:53.759
...I saw you as my only way out.

00:50:55.010 --> 00:50:58.179
No, Heeju, it's okay. We can be happy like before.

00:50:58.180 --> 00:51:00.849
That money will fix everything. What more could we need?

00:51:04.395 --> 00:51:05.646
Yangpo is out.

00:51:06.230 --> 00:51:08.274
They've tightened up security. It's too risky.

00:51:09.650 --> 00:51:12.319
So I was thinking a boat might be our best bet.

00:51:13.529 --> 00:51:14.655
We stowaway?

00:51:15.281 --> 00:51:16.282
Mm-hmm.

00:51:17.241 --> 00:51:20.494
I know someone who uses cargo ships to export cars.

00:51:22.162 --> 00:51:23.539
How do you know them?

00:51:25.583 --> 00:51:27.418
Turns out money can do anything.

00:51:27.918 --> 00:51:30.588
Okay, then. Let's move as quickly as possible.

00:51:31.088 --> 00:51:33.215
No, I'm not going with you.

00:51:33.757 --> 00:51:35.009
You're going by yourself.

00:51:35.593 --> 00:51:37.386
And the gold bars...

00:51:39.221 --> 00:51:40.431
...we should split them.

00:51:41.015 --> 00:51:42.016
What?

00:51:42.683 --> 00:51:43.684
I...

00:51:44.602 --> 00:51:47.145
I think I deserve at least that much. Don't you?

00:51:47.146 --> 00:51:50.357
I risked my life to keep them hidden. So here's what we'll do.

00:51:50.983 --> 00:51:55.111
On the day you head for Cambodia, I'll bring your share by car.

00:51:55.112 --> 00:51:56.904
I'll bring your passport, too.

00:51:56.905 --> 00:51:58.782
So you can just meet me at the port.

00:52:00.618 --> 00:52:02.952
And you won't try and find the rest of the gold bars.

00:52:02.953 --> 00:52:05.163
What? Heeju. What are you talking about?

00:52:05.164 --> 00:52:07.290
Look, tell me where you are.

00:52:07.291 --> 00:52:08.667
Can we please just talk about this in person?

00:52:09.418 --> 00:52:10.502
Whatever you say.

00:52:11.045 --> 00:52:13.379
We can just split the gold bars, if that's what you want.

00:52:13.380 --> 00:52:15.049
But can we at least talk in person?

00:52:15.591 --> 00:52:16.799
Where are you now?

00:52:16.800 --> 00:52:18.343
Are you still staying at the pawnshop?

00:52:18.344 --> 00:52:20.262
No, I'm not there anymore.

00:52:20.888 --> 00:52:22.014
Don't go there.

00:52:22.598 --> 00:52:24.558
And don't come looking for me, either.

00:52:27.102 --> 00:52:28.771
Wait, Hee-Heeju.

00:52:35.569 --> 00:52:37.988
INCOMING CALL

00:52:44.453 --> 00:52:45.995
POWER OFF

00:53:00.302 --> 00:53:03.137
Your call has been forwarded to an automated voice-

00:53:05.933 --> 00:53:08.351
Fuck! Why are you doing this?

00:53:12.940 --> 00:53:14.400
:cue

00:53:26.161 --> 00:53:27.745
Boss.

00:53:27.746 --> 00:53:29.206
I want to repay you for everything.

00:53:29.998 --> 00:53:33.752
I know this isn't anything special, but I made it for you.

00:53:34.253 --> 00:53:35.254
Here.

00:53:37.172 --> 00:53:39.508
It's a four-leaf clover. It brings good luck.

00:53:41.135 --> 00:53:44.680
So if you wear it then you'll be lucky.

00:53:46.849 --> 00:53:49.559
Oh, I made it with my own share of the potatoes,

00:53:49.560 --> 00:53:51.520
so you don't have to worry about that.

00:53:53.230 --> 00:53:54.480
Is that true?

00:53:54.481 --> 00:53:55.482
What?

00:53:56.442 --> 00:53:57.693
If I keep this with me...

00:53:59.653 --> 00:54:02.114
...will it really bring good luck, even to me?

00:54:02.698 --> 00:54:05.325
Um, well, no.

00:54:05.909 --> 00:54:08.494
It's just a superstition, of course.

00:54:08.495 --> 00:54:13.625
But believing in things like that can still bring us comfort.

00:54:24.511 --> 00:54:25.512
Thank you.

00:54:26.513 --> 00:54:29.475
Take care of yourself, Heeju.

00:54:41.612 --> 00:54:43.738
All right. So what'd he say?

00:54:56.460 --> 00:54:57.628
By the way.

00:54:59.171 --> 00:55:02.256
Heeju, do you have to go this far?

00:55:02.257 --> 00:55:03.717
Just for Lee Dokyung?

00:55:04.801 --> 00:55:06.678
I mean, you're helping with his travel.

00:55:08.388 --> 00:55:10.182
And giving him half of the gold bars, too.

00:55:13.685 --> 00:55:16.438
I just, I overheard you talking on the phone yesterday.

00:55:17.397 --> 00:55:19.107
It's not like I meant to.

00:55:19.358 --> 00:55:21.317
It was an accident! It was.

00:55:21.318 --> 00:55:23.903
I went back to grab something I left and I heard you.

00:55:23.904 --> 00:55:25.989
It really, really was an accident.

00:55:30.536 --> 00:55:32.079
It was his to begin with.

00:55:32.788 --> 00:55:35.331
I figured I should give him his share.

00:55:35.332 --> 00:55:37.625
Lee Dokyung's share is half of the bars?

00:55:37.626 --> 00:55:38.961
Really?

00:55:39.545 --> 00:55:41.003
Heeju, do you-

00:55:41.004 --> 00:55:42.548
do you still love that asshole?

00:55:43.090 --> 00:55:45.716
Huh? Even after everything he did to you?

00:55:45.717 --> 00:55:47.219
Didn't you break up already?

00:55:48.387 --> 00:55:49.513
Yeah, we did.

00:55:53.058 --> 00:55:54.268
We're breaking up.

00:55:55.435 --> 00:55:58.104
But it's not like I want him to be unhappy.

00:55:58.105 --> 00:55:59.690
What does that even mean?

00:56:00.941 --> 00:56:02.942
Ugh, I don't know. Leave me alone.

00:56:02.943 --> 00:56:04.193
It's my gold anyway.

00:56:04.194 --> 00:56:05.404
No, it's mine, too!

00:56:06.446 --> 00:56:09.116
Of those 100 gold bars, 5% belongs to me.

00:56:10.492 --> 00:56:12.368
You're just gonna give half to Dokyung?

00:56:12.369 --> 00:56:13.370
Okay, then.

00:56:13.829 --> 00:56:15.664
You can have 10% of my share.

00:56:16.248 --> 00:56:19.751
For every ten-kilo gold bar I cash in, you get a one-kilo bar.

00:56:20.043 --> 00:56:21.044
Sound good?

00:56:25.424 --> 00:56:27.384
Wait a minute. Let me just do the math.

00:56:28.010 --> 00:56:29.636
Four, five, six, seven.

00:56:30.679 --> 00:56:32.556
Ten billion?

00:56:34.558 --> 00:56:35.642
I get ten billion?

00:56:39.688 --> 00:56:43.525
Wow! Ten bill! Fuck me!

00:56:44.067 --> 00:56:45.777
Is that enough for you?

00:56:46.278 --> 00:56:47.738
That's all you've ever wanted? :cue

00:56:49.156 --> 00:56:50.991
Why?

00:56:52.784 --> 00:56:54.161
Will you give me more if I ask?

00:56:56.496 --> 00:56:58.081
No, I was just wondering.

00:56:58.665 --> 00:57:00.292
You'd do anything for money.

00:57:00.751 --> 00:57:02.502
Yet you've been the least greedy.

00:57:04.046 --> 00:57:08.050
Every other person around me has tried to steal everything I had.

00:57:09.384 --> 00:57:11.803
Really? Huh. I, uh, never thought about it.

00:57:32.491 --> 00:57:34.700
Hi, good evening. Did you order express delivery?

00:57:34.701 --> 00:57:35.785
Yeah.

00:57:35.786 --> 00:57:36.828
Okay.

00:58:08.860 --> 00:58:11.404
HAENGBOK PAWNSHOP

00:58:55.282 --> 00:58:56.283
Fuck.

01:00:06.478 --> 01:00:07.479
Why are you here?

01:00:08.647 --> 01:00:09.689
H-Heeju.

